Package: swissValet
Type: Package
Title: Interactive Functions to be Used as Shortcuts in 'RStudio'
Version: 0.0.0.908
Authors@R: person(given = "Andri",
                  family = "Signorell",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "andri@signorell.net",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4311-1969"))
Description: Provides addins for 'RStudio' that apply frequently needed
    inspection functions to the current editor selection and execute
    them in the console, among them str(), example(), plot(), head(),
    summary() and unclass(). Assigning keyboard shortcuts to these
    addins turns a repeated select-copy-wrap-run cycle into a single
    keystroke. The package further contains interactive Tcl/Tk dialogs
    for selecting variables and for sorting code elements, converters
    between Unicode characters and escape sequences, and a routine that
    writes a selected object back into the editor as reproducible
    source code.
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: stats, DescToolsX, pharos, bedrock, rstudioapi (>= 0.1), 
         writexl, foreign, tools, tcltk, cli, clipr
Remotes: 
    AndriSignorell/bedrock, AndriSignorell/DescToolsX, AndriSignorell/pharos 
